WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.566 --> 00:00:10.199
[Heredity]

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:26.440
[Narrator:] It has long been observed that like tends to beget like.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.633
However, there are variations within most animal groups and some of these have a hereditary basis.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.860
Let us follow a simple case of inheritance in short-horns.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.160
A pure-breeding red male produces sperms,

00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:54.532
each of which carries in one of its chromosomes a hereditary unit or gene for red coat.

00:00:54.533 --> 00:00:59.133
This, we shall indicate by a black dot.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.400
A pure-breeding white short-horn female, produces eggs,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.500
each of which carries in one of its chromosomes a gene for white coat.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:16.700
This we shall indicate by a white dot.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:23.633
Thus, from a mating between a pure-breeding red male, and a pure-breeding white female,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:34.140
every fertilized egg or zygote, will have one gene for red coat, and one gene for white coat.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:39.440
A zygote divides by a type of cell division called mitosis.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:44.040
In this type of division, the chromosomes arrange themselves along the centers,

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.460
then the chromosomes and their genes duplicate themselves.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:58.200
Of the two sets of chromosomes formed, one set moves to each daughter cell.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:08.980
Note that each daughter cell contains the same hereditary materials as did the mother cell.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:16.900
Since all cells of the body are formed in this way, each cell of the offspring contains a red gene and a white,

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.440
as did the zygote from which they came.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:28.333
Due to the influence of both genes, the calf will be roan.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:32.980
Let us now cross two roan animals.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:41.200
When a body cell gives rise to sperms or eggs, the chromosomes pair off instead of lining up individually.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.400
One chromosome of each pair goes to each daughter cell.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.160
Thus, a roan male produces two kinds of sperm.

00:02:50.166 --> 00:02:54.766
...gene for red coat, and one a gene for white.

00:02:54.766 --> 00:03:03.000
Similarly, a roan female produces two kinds of eggs.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.520
In mating, there's a random combination of sperms and eggs.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:11.800
This sperm may unite with this egg to form a red-red zygote,

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:16.920
which will give rise to a red calf.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:28.220
Or, it may unite with this egg to form a red-white zygote, which will give rise to a roan calf.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:42.000
This sperm may unite with this egg to form a white-red zygote, which also will develop into a roan calf.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.433
Or, it may unite with this egg to form a white-white zygote,

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:52.460
which will give rise to a white calf.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:04:08.820
Thus, from a roan by roan cross, we may expect 1/4 of the offspring to be red, 2/4 roan, and 1/4 white.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:14.433
Guinea pig crosses gives slightly different end results.

00:04:14.433 --> 00:04:22.866
A pure-breeding black male Guinea pig produces sperms, all of which carry a gene for black coat.

00:04:22.866 --> 00:04:33.600
A pure-breeding white female produces eggs, all of which carry a gene for white coat.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:44.200
Hence, all zygotes resulting from such a cross will have a gene for black coat and a gene for white.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:52.933
Since the zygote divides by mitosis, all the body cells will have both a black gene and a white.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:58.980
In the determination of coat color, the black gene dominates over the white.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:06.333
Consequently, the individual will be black.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.533
Now, let us cross two such black Guinea pigs.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:18.033
This black male with cells like this produces sperms, half of which carry the black gene,

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:24.133
and half of which carry the white gene.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:31.020
Similarly, the black female produces two kinds of eggs.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:38.860
In mating, this sperm may unite with this egg, or it may unite with this egg.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:47.060
This sperm may unite with this egg, or it may unite with this egg.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:52.200
Of the zygotes produced, three will carry at least one black gene.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.400
One will lack a black gene.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:06:05.620
Due to dominance of black, 3/4 will be black, and 1/4 white.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:08.760
Rough coat in Guinea pigs is also inherited.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:15.080
When a pure rough-coated male is crossed with a pure smooth female,

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:20.080
every zygote will have a rough gene and a smooth gene.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.733
Rough is dominant over smooth.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:25.233
Consequently, all the immediate offspring will be rough.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:36.033
A mating between two such rough Guinea pigs will give three rough to one smooth.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:45.300
Let us now cross a pure-breeding black rough male and a pure-breeding white smooth female.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:52.760
Each sperm of a black rough male will carry a black gene, and a rough gene.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:07:02.233
Each egg will carry a white gene and a smooth gene.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:08.960
Consequently, every zygote from such a cross will carry each of the four genes:

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.320
black, white, rough, and smooth.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:16.360
Due to the dominance of the black gene and the rough gene,

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:25.900
every zygote from this cross will develop into a black rough Guinea pig.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:31.560
Let us now cross two such black rough Guinea pigs.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:39.340
When a black rough male produces sperm, the chromosomes may orient themselves in two different ways.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:50.180
In one, the black gene and the rough gene may go to one sperm, while the white gene and the smooth gene go to the other.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:08:00.640
In the other possible way, the black gene and the smooth gene may go to one sperm,

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:06.720
while the white gene and the rough gene go to the other.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:15.500
Thus, a black rough male will produce four times the sperms in equal numbers.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:24.640
Similarly, a black rough female will produce four kinds of eggs in equal numbers.

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:34.040
The black rough sperm may unite with each of the four kinds of eggs.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:41.400
The black smooth sperm may unite with each of the four kinds of eggs.

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:48.560
The white rough sperm may unite with each of the four kinds of eggs.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:56.400
The white smooth sperm may unite with each of the four kinds of eggs.

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:05.940
Of the 16 possible combinations, nine will have at least one black gene and one rough gene.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:10.080
Due to dominance, these offspring will be black rough.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.860
Three will have at least one black gene, but no rough gene.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.520
These will be black smooth.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:25.400
Three will have no black genes, but at least one rough gene.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:28.780
These will be white, rough.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:36.500
One will have no black and no rough gene.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:40.960
And this will be white, smooth.

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:56.360
Only when many litters are combined may one expect this theoretical 9:3:3:1 ratio.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:04.233
In this film, we have shown schematically the mode of transmission of the hereditary materials

00:10:04.233 --> 00:10:13.266
which are responsible for the inherited characters of all plants and animals.

